	<!-- About screen -->
	<string name="about_title">About</string>
	<string name="about_version_format">Version %1$s</string>
	<string name="about_story_title">About the project</string>
	<string name="about_story_p1">VzSync is a personal project created by Vtzin x with a simple goal: sending folders and files to GitHub repositories with a single tap, without typing commands in a terminal.</string>
	<string name="about_story_p2">The idea came from a real problem. Vtzin x programs directly from his phone, editing projects in a mobile editor, using Termux to run Git commands, and setting up GitHub Actions to build the project. With every small change, the same ritual had to be repeated: open the terminal, type git add, git commit, git push — several times a day.</string>
	<string name="about_story_p3">VzSync exists to eliminate that friction. It\'s one of those projects born to solve a personal annoyance that, for that very reason, ends up helping anyone facing the same situation. That\'s the philosophy behind VzTechCore: tools that help the author and, as a bonus, anyone with the same need.</string>
	<string name="about_story_p4">Independently developed, with care and without rush, VzSync keeps evolving. It\'s the kind of project that starts small but solves a big problem for those who code from their phone.</string>
